+# RPi4 USB initialization investigation / 2026-10-11
+
+Source: main `a094b953c`, USB source `8c93ba8e0`. Current user requested config and initialization investigation. This is read-only source/artifact investigation, not a new implementation Queue.
+
+## Physical report
+
+User reports USB keyboard and USB LAN unavailable, unplug/replug produces no visible messages. USB messages were not observed; absence of PCIe messages is uncertain. No usable Ethernet/input for dmesg. USB previously worked; the working image/commit is unidentified. This is failed physical acceptance of p009.
+
+## Verified findings
+
+- Actual Make evaluation with current config selects rpi4/arm64, xHCI/HID/hub/storage and graphical login. USB core/xHCI sources are selected. Main kernel.elf disassembly of drv_rpi4_pcie_init contains USB core initialization, flag store, log call and class registrations.
+- Boot worker retains the original extended handoff, discovers then refreshes devices before VFS/userspace. RPi4 runs SDHCI, PCIe then VC4. Reaching SD login rules out earlier SDHCI exits on this path.
+- USB core/class/xHCI registration precedes FDT/controller/link checks. Missing or disabled PCIe cannot itself skip the core call. No earlier RPi4 USB core caller found.
+- Initialization sequence: runtime FDT → controller description → reset/SerDes → DMA window → link training → outbound window/BAR allocation → VL805 firmware mailbox/reassignment → PCI scan → xHCI attach/start → worker → platform refresh enables root probing → VFS input-ready activates pending HID.
+- The checked-in firmware DTB enables BCM2711 PCIe and contains expected ranges/reset node. Runtime firmware can mutate this tree; runtime contents are unverified.
+- brcmstb ops do not set defer_unassigned, so PCI deferred probing does not hold this host back.
+- Platform discards PCIe initialization errors; PCI enumeration can succeed despite endpoint attach failure. Login therefore does not prove a usable USB host.
+- Early screen messages can scroll away or be cleared on VC4 console repaint/takeover, while the log retains them. Screen absence alone does not establish skipped initialization.
+- USB core EALREADY currently stops class registration, but no earlier caller found: robustness observation only, not established cause.
+- xHCI worker polls topology every 100 ms once root_ready is set. Keyboard and LAN both failing is consistent with common host failure, without identifying the stage.
+
+## Evidence recovery / resume
+
+Existing syslogd copies boot/current kernel records to `/var/log/kernel.log`, follows and flushes every two seconds, and keeps `/var/log/kernel.log.old` from the previous boot. If syslogd starts and storage is writable, the SD system partition supplies logs without keyboard/SSH. User will attach data.img; recover logs read-only once received. Image not yet received. `/run/dmesg.boot` is also generated but may be volatile.
+
+No source edits, builds, QEMU, hardware access, push or main integration. Root cause remains unconfirmed. Resume with kernel log/serial evidence or identified working image; inspect the first PCIe/xHCI failure. Logo/kernel animation stays deferred. Shared projections/GitHub pending Q1.
+
+## Photo and attached data image follow-up
+
+User supplied photo shows `usb: URB completion contract q009-release-acquire-v1`, brcmstb resetting at fd500000, revision 304, link up generation 2 x1, and 01:00.0 BAR0 at c0000000 (4096 bytes). User confirms this screen later advances to login. USB core initialization, controller reset, PCIe link and initial BAR assignment have physical evidence. No firmware/xHCI outcome is visible in this photo; it does not locate a permanent stop.
+
+Attached data.img: 33554432 bytes, SHA256 e9934e45b34599b0176137b2a58e98e7458b038709d4abe81534c7268c0d90b6. Read-only `file`, `fls -r -p`, `istat`, `icat` and checked-in UFS reader agree: only /.zovl0, /.zovl1 and /etc/zedbsd-root; no /var or logs. No writes/mounts performed. Current RPi4 image includes a separate native UFS root partition, selected before legacy image overlay by vfs_mount_legacy_root; data.img is not the current root/log storage. Corrected the earlier acquisition advice to the user; requested /var/log/kernel.log from the booted SD second partition or booted SD whole-card image.
+
+Additional static observation: firmware wait_mailbox counts 100000 10us sleeps as a nominal one-second timeout. Current kern_usleep_range yields until a scheduler tick and may exceed the requested interval; RPi4 reports 1ms ticks. This timeout may therefore take much longer than one second. Nested waits also restart the budget on unrelated mailbox words. This is a timing defect in the nominal timeout contract, not yet evidence of the actual USB failure or firmware response absence. No source change under this read-only investigation.
+
+## Storage-layout clarification / 2026-10-11
+
+User reports no apparent second partition and expects loopback mounting, then asks whether migration is complete. Verified current main build/arm64/hdd-image.img MBR directly: partition1 type0x0c, LBA2048, 134217728 bytes; partition2 type0xa5, LBA264192, 207618048 bytes. Current generator is native UFS root; vfs_mount_legacy_root retains loopback overlay fallback when no marked UFS partition exists. This proves the locally generated image layout only. Actual physical-card partition table/root selection remains unverified; earlier statements that the actual card uses native UFS are corrected. Attached data.img genuinely has no logs; absence does not itself prove root selection or a storage failure. Need actual card evidence before further location claims.
